    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d118">

                <pb facs="0289" n="175" sameAs="frus:frus1931v01/pg175"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">462.00R296/4094: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Belgium</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Mayer</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Brussels</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-06-25T11:00:00+01:00">June 25, 1931—11
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received June 25—7:14 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>53. Department’s 34 [<hi rendition="#italic">37?</hi>], June 24, 11 p.m.<anchor
                        n="59" xml:id="d118-f1"/> Does the President’s proposal apply to Belgium
                    equally as to France or is Belgium not to be considered as one of the “important
                    creditor countries” who are to postpone debt and reparations receipts for one
                    year.</p>
                <p>If the latter is the case suggest I be given immediate authorization so to inform
                    Foreign Office. Urgent reply by telegraph respectfully requested.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mayer</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
